Description: Fits a joint model for Likert-type item responses and item
    response times in which responses follow Samejima's (1969)
    <doi:10.1007/BF03372160> graded response model and log response times
    follow a distance-difficulty (inverted-U) model, so that responding is
    slowest when a respondent's trait level is close to the item location
    (Ferrando and Lorenzo-Seva, 2007 <doi:10.1177/0146621606295197>; Molenaar
    et al., 2021 <doi:10.1177/0146621621990756>). Estimation is by marginal
    maximum likelihood with an EM algorithm, with normal or robust Student-t
    errors for noisy web-survey timings, symmetric or asymmetric distance
    slopes, item-level Wald and likelihood-ratio tests of the
    distance-difficulty effect, and trait scores that use response times as
    collateral information.
